+Config (`.env`): `HOSTINGER_API`, `PF_VPS_ID`, `PF_DOMAIN`, `PF_PROJECT`, `PF_GIT_URL`, `PF_GIT_REF`, `TELESCOPE_ENABLED`, `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`, `DISCORD_MENTION_ID`, `LOG_STACK`, `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS`.
 
 ## Discord ops alerts
 
@@ -69,8 +69,11 @@ ## Discord ops alerts
 | Env | `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` → `config('services.discord.webhook_url')` |
 | Client | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send($title, $message, $context = [])` |
 | Unconfigured | Empty/missing URL → silent no-op (safe for CI) |
+| Mention | `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` → `config('services.discord.mention_id')`; a Discord user ID pinged on every alert (see below) |
 | Failures | Non-2xx / transport errors are logged without the webhook URL; they do not throw |
 
+**On-call ping:** when `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` is a Discord user ID (snowflake: 17–20 digits, surrounding whitespace trimmed), every alert ends with `<@ID>` on its own line so the on-call person gets a push notification. Empty or any other value (`@everyone`, `@here`, names, values with newlines or extra characters) adds no mention. The 1800-character limit applies to the whole content: when an alert is truncated, the title/message/context are cut first so the mention survives. Only a single user is supported; role and `@everyone` mentions are never emitted.
+
 Call from jobs/handlers when a notable ops event occurs; do not wire every exception globally.
 
 ```php
